"IETF itself also carries out problematic modifications. For example, in
May 2025, IESG posted an IESG-mangled version of an appeal that I had
filed, and then in its response confused exactly the point obfuscated by
that mangling. When I complained about the mangled document, the IETF
Executive Director responded not by apologizing but instead by asserting
that IETF management had the power to do whatever it wanted."=
